#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""ot-heavy-reconcile v17 (hard invariant, see below; header text from v13): keep ot-heavy reservations at MEASURED memory use, and learn sizes per command class.

ot-heavy charges every running job `reservation - current use` of future growth.  This pass (cron, every 5 min, all
hosts) lowers a reservation to ceil(max(peak * 1.25, peak + 4 GB)) once the job is provably past its memory peak:

  sim    the scope holds only a Verilator/vvp simulation binary (plus shell wrappers), seen on two passes: the build is
         finished.  peak = max(sum VmHWM of the live processes, largest sample).
  route  every docker container of the scope shows detail routing begun (global placement and GRT are behind it).
         peak = the cgroups' memory.peak.
  flat   nothing is compiling / synthesising, no container is in global placement or GRT, and the job's RSS (scope +
         its containers) has been flat for FLAT_S = 10 min.  peak = max(sum VmHWM, largest sample).

Never lowered: a job with a compiler / Verilator / yosys / make process, a flow container not yet in detail route, a
bare OpenROAD container whose fresh logs show GPL/GRT activity.  A lowered unit that starts building again or grows past
80 % of its lowered reservation gets its launch value back.  cgroup limits and processes are never touched.

It also writes use.<unit> (GB held by the unit's docker containers, which the scope's MemoryCurrent does not see, so
ot-heavy stops charging that memory twice), appends every finished unit's peak to peaks.tsv and rebuilds sizes.json
(class -> measured peak).

v3 (owner 2026-10-13, admission by memory only): a request above 2x the measured peak of its class is CHARGED
ceil(max(1.5 x peak, peak + 8 GB)) -- by `ot-heavy` at admission (--admit) and, for a unit that was admitted at its full
request, by this pass (LOWER ... (class)).  A class counts once it has a finished job (n) or a live job this pass proved
past its peak (proved); the local table is merged with sizes.fleet.json (all hosts, written by tools/fleet/ot-sizes-sync).
The unit's MemoryMax stays the request; a class-sized unit gets its request back when its RSS passes 80 % of the charge
(building alone does not restore it: the class peak already contains the build).

v4 (coordinator 2026-10-13 07:40, reservations again held 690-800 GB of 830-870 GB available on the EPYCs): the gate
families FAST (ref_gate_*, view_export*, run_case*, relay_*) are lowered to ceil(max(1.25 x peak, peak + 4 GB)) after
FAST_S = 3 min of flat RSS whatever runs inside (their class key carries the element name, so a new element was a new,
unproved class and kept its 24 GB for the whole gate); restored at RSS > 80 % of the charge.  SEED: a ref_gate_* request
whose own class has no measurement is charged 10 GB at admission (the family measures 0.6-7.3 GB).  cron: every 2 min.

v6 (owner 2026-10-13 17:55, "books far from reality, in opposite directions on the two big hosts"): ONE arithmetic,
books(), for admission (`ot-heavy` calls --gate), for placement (--free, read by ot-run) and for --units.  Before, --free
charged every unit `reservation - use` (EPYC1: 900 GB of growth against 592 GB available, "free -382 GB") while ot-heavy
capped the same growth from the observed peak and went on admitting, and a unit younger than 5 min was charged its whole
request (EPYC4: three 70 GB builds held 720 GB and a 48 GB job queued at 806 GB available); ot-heavy-trim, which was to
lower those, never ran from cron (no XDG_RUNTIME_DIR, so every unit looked inactive) and is retired.  The rule:
  charge(unit) = what it can still grow into = min(target, ceiling) - memory it holds now
    now      memory it holds (scope cgroup + its docker containers)
    target   age >= 30 min: now + max(now/4, 2 GB);  >= 5 min: now + max(now/2, 4 GB);  never above 1.1 x the measured
             peak of its class + 2 GB while it is below that peak;  younger than 5 min: now + 8 GB when the host is in
             PLENTY, else its expected size (1.1 x class peak, or half the request when the class is not measured)
             (the margin follows what the unit holds NOW, not its peak: a build that peaked at 57 GB in Verilator and
             runs its simulation at 4 GB was charged as if it would take the 57 GB again, 5 x 70 GB on EPYC1)
    ceiling  its MemoryMax (the request); the reservation file when reconcile lowered it and RSS is below 80 % of it
    PLENTY   MemAvailable - (expected size not yet taken by the units younger than 5 min) >= 35 % of RAM
  admit(RES) iff MemAvailable - RES >= FLOOR (20 % of RAM, the safety stop) and either
    books:  MemAvailable - sum(charge) - HEADROOM >= RES, or
    real:   MemAvailable - young >= 25 % of RAM and MemAvailable - young - RES >= FLOOR   (young = expected size not yet
            taken by units younger than 5 min: the only memory MemAvailable cannot show yet)
  so no request waits while more than 25 % of RAM is really available unless it does not fit above the floor.
A reservation whose scope is gone is charged for 20 s only (was 120 s: every finished 12-16 GB docker step of the loop
stayed on the books for two minutes).

v8 admission (owner 2026-10-17: "as long as the current memory is enough, you should not reserve a very large amount of
memory because the server can auto swap and the reservations often have too large margins. The fleet should admit the
tasks as soon as possible"):
  charge(unit) = min(the v6 charge above, GROWTH_FACTOR x (declared ceiling - memory it holds now))
                 (a reservation admitted but not started yet: GROWTH_FACTOR x its reservation)
  admit(RES) iff MemAvailable - sum(charge) >= NEED_FACTOR x RES  and  MemAvailable - NEED_FACTOR x RES >= MIN_AVAIL_FRAC x RAM
  HEADROOM_GB, the 20 % floor and the 25 % rule no longer apply to the gate (HEADROOM_GB stays only in ot-heavy's bash
  fallback for when this script cannot answer).  admit_gb (--free, ot-run) is the largest DECLARED request admitted now.
  Config (/etc/ot-heavy.conf, KEY=value; the environment overrides):  GROWTH_FACTOR=0.5  NEED_FACTOR=0.7
  MIN_AVAIL_FRAC=0.05 (just above earlyoom's 3 % kill line; REAL_FLOOR_GB=<GB> overrides it absolutely).
  v11 (2026-10-21): admission charges the sum of every running unit's supported future growth. The former
  aggregate cap of 10 % of RAM hid concurrent young jobs' growth and let five 64 GB replays trigger host earlyoom.
  v12 GROWING RESERVATION (SCHED-MEM 2026-10-21, EP7 11:52:52-11:53:13: five 64 GB replays admitted in 21 s against
  188 GB available, each matured to 38.5 GB, earlyoom TERMed the paused 490 GB TP192 build): a unit admitted in the last
  GROW_WINDOW_S (default 600 s) or still GROWING (a compiler/Verilator/yosys process in it, or its RSS rose over the last
  reconcile samples, and reconcile has not proved it past its peak) is charged its WHOLE remaining reservation,
  ceiling - memory it holds now (GROWING_FACTOR, default 1.0, replaces GROWTH_FACTOR for those units), and a reservation
  admitted but not started is charged in full while its ot-heavy launcher lives.  These pending charges are summed over
  every such unit and are also charged to die jobs (DIE "current memory" = MemAvailable - pending), since MemAvailable
  cannot show memory promised a moment ago.  Older settled units keep the v8 GROWTH_FACTOR rule.  --gate takes the
  admission lock itself when its caller (ot-heavy holds fd 8) does not, so concurrent admissions cannot race.
  v13 GROWTH RATE (SCHED-TUNE 2026-10-21 12:29: v12 charged ot-epyc5 817 GB of growth at load 25 with 929 GB available,
  admitting 160 GB: every old job with a compiler process -- a 34 h yosys at 7 GB, a 13 h die job at 88 GB of 700 --
  counted as GROWING and was charged its whole --mem, and s["samples"] is wiped on each building/GRT pass, so no RSS delta
  was ever recorded).  reconcile now keeps rss_hist (the last 3 cron samples, never reset) and rate_gbs.  Charge:
    admitted < GROW_WINDOW_S (600 s) ago, or no reconcile sample yet (still building):  ceiling - now (as v12)
    RSS rose > max(5 %, 0.5 GiB) between the last two cron samples:  min(ceiling - now, RATE_MULT (2) x rate x
      RATE_HORIZON_S (600 s))
    stable or old:  0, plus one host floor min(sum of their (ceiling - now), SETTLED_FLOOR_FRAC (0.02) x RAM)
  The v6/v8 age/class/GROWTH_FACTOR rules above no longer set the charge (GROWTH_FACTOR is read but unused).
  Active Verilator frontend phases (verified executable in the scope's current cgroup) retain full declared
  remaining growth until the frontend exits. Flat RSS or a lowered class reservation cannot predict its next AST phase.
  Other sampled phases keep the v13 rate policy; this does not restore full reservations for long-running yosys jobs.
  v14 OLD SLOW (SCHED-TUNE2, owner 2026-10-22: gold2 showed admits -55 GB with 436 GB free at load 32/112 because
  6-15 h cc1plus compiles at 54-87 GB, growing a few MB per sample, each held its whole declared --mem through the
  frontend-phase rule while its verilator_bin only waited on its --build): a unit older than OLD_S (7200 s) whose
  measured growth is below OLD_SLOW_GB (5 GB) per 10 min and whose every verilator_bin pid has a make/compiler
  descendant is charged min(ceiling - now, OLD_MULT (3) x rate x OLD_HORIZON_S (1800 s), OLD_CAP_GB (32)).  rate = RSS
  slope over rss_hist (now kept 30 min, not 3 samples), never below the last-two-sample v13 rate.  A frontend still in
  its AST phase keeps the full declared charge (13:01 TP192 grew again after a plateau); other units keep v13 (stable 0;
  rising 2 x rate x 600 s, already under the v14 charge below 5 GB/10 min), so v14 never charges more than v13.
  Young units, the host floor, the settled floor, the admit lock and the 5 x 64 GB replay regression are unchanged.
  v15 BUILD WAIT (SCHED-TUNE2 10-22 05:38: ep9 charged 253 GB to a 1.8 h K_cut_7 whose frontend had peaked at 234 GB
  and only waited on eight 2-11 GB cc1plus): the build-waiting charge applies from GROW_WINDOW_S (OLD_S 7200 -> 600);
  growth >= OLD_SLOW_GB/10 min is charged the v13 rate rule min(margin, 2 x rate x 600 s) instead of the full remainder.
  AST-phase frontends (incl. hierarchical sub-frontends under make) still keep their full declared charge.
  Safety stays with the per-job caps (scope MemoryMax, docker --memory via ot-heavy-docker), swap and earlyoom.
  DIE-FIRST unchanged: a waiting die trial's request is held free against non-die requests.

v17 HARD INVARIANT (S81c coordinator / TOKc-ADM 2026-10-22: earlyoom killed 44 GB cc1plus on ep5 11:54-11:56 and
14:15-14:22 and on gold2 13:07 at MemAvailable 3 % / swap 100 % while every scope was under its own cap; ep5 14:12:15-30
admitted five run_dv_slice.sh builds, 896 GB declared, against 291-279 GB available because v16 put the fresh charges
inside the 25 %-of-MemAvailable growth cap).  On top of every rule above, for non-die AND die requests:
    committed = other + sum(max(now, peak so far)) + reserve (v16 running growth) + fresh (unstarted / < 5 min)
    admit(RES) only if committed + RES <= MemTotal - INV_HEADROOM_GB (64); nothing while committed > MemTotal - 64
  (see invariant()).  --free reports admit_gb / die_admit_gb already bounded by it, plus inv_free_gb and committed_gb.
  HARD_INVARIANT=0 in /etc/ot-heavy.conf disables it.  --exit-report (called by ot-heavy-exit inside every scope when the
  command ends non-zero) prints EARLYOOM / MEMCG-OOM lines for kills of the job's processes.

v9 (owner 2026-10-18 ~01:05 "NEVER hold jobs on CPU load; keep the fleet busy; never hold important jobs"; memory 10-08:
priority must never leave a host idle):
  DIE-FIRST v2 = ORDER, not reservation: a non-die request yields only to a waiting die job that the host admits NOW
  (charge <= its admissible; it starts on its next attempt, ot-heavy re-tries die waiters every 5 s).  A die job is
  admitted on CURRENT memory alone (MemAvailable - NEED_FACTOR x request >= floor; running units' growth is not charged:
  owner 10-17 "admit as soon as current memory suffices; swap is the safety net", 10-18 "never hold important jobs").  A die job that does
  not fit now holds nothing, so small jobs keep running (v8 held a 48 GB die charge on AGIdock while 75 waiters sat at
  load 13/64).  Die-level = OT_HEAVY_PRIO=die, or the command / its cwd matches DIE_RE or a line of PRIO_FILE
  (/var/tmp/ot-heavy/prio_die.re, one regex per line: marks waiters already queued, read on every attempt).
  --free reports load as cpu_load1 (ot-run v6 orders by it and never holds; the v5 hold read "load1", so v5 clients
  still running stop holding once this is deployed).

usage: ot-heavy-reconcile [--dry-run] [--verbose]     one pass
       ot-heavy-reconcile --units                      table: request, charge, growth, now, peak, class peak, age per unit
       ot-heavy-reconcile --gate MEM -- CMD...         "OK|NO <charged GB> <class> | <arithmetic>" (ot-heavy, under its lock)
       ot-heavy-reconcile --selftest                   the charge and admission rules on synthetic units
       ot-heavy-reconcile --free [DIR]                 JSON: memory free after reservations, waiters, disk (for ot-run)
       ot-heavy-reconcile --sizes                      print the learned table
       ot-heavy-reconcile --exit-report UNIT T0 RC PIDFILE [CG]   EARLYOOM / MEMCG-OOM lines for a finished job (v17)
       ot-heavy-reconcile --size MEM -- CMD...         print a warning line if MEM > 2x the measured peak of CMD's class
       ot-heavy-reconcile --admit MEM -- CMD...        print "<GB> <why>" when MEM is charged less than requested
"""
import calendar, fcntl, glob, json, math, os, re, subprocess, sys, time

os.environ.setdefault("XDG_RUNTIME_DIR", f"/run/user/{os.getuid()}")   # cron has none; systemctl --user needs it
D = "/var/tmp/ot-heavy"
STATE, LOG, LOCK = f"{D}/reconcile.state.json", f"{D}/reconcile.log", f"{D}/admit.lock"
PEAKS, SIZES, FLEET = f"{D}/peaks.tsv", f"{D}/sizes.json", f"{D}/sizes.fleet.json"
FLAT_S = 10 * 60
FAST_S = 3 * 60
FAST = re.compile(r"^(ref_gate_|view_export|run_case|relay_)")
SEED = {"ref_gate_": 10}          # GB charged at first sight when the exact class has no measurement yet
GB = 1 << 30
WRAPPERS = {"bash", "sh", "dash", "tee", "tail", "time", "env", "timeout", "stdbuf", "nice", "cat", "sleep", "docker",
            "tini", "docker-init", "ot-heavy-exit", "sort"}   # v17: ot-heavy-exit + its pid sampler sit in every scope
BUILD = {"cc1plus", "cc1", "g++", "gcc", "c++", "clang", "clang++", "ld", "collect2", "lto1", "as", "ar", "make", "ninja",
         "cmake", "verilator", "verilator_bin", "iverilog", "ivl", "yosys", "yosys-abc", "abc"}
DRY, VERBOSE = "--dry-run" in sys.argv, "--verbose" in sys.argv or "--dry-run" in sys.argv
NOW = time.time()


def log(m):
    line = f"{time.strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S%z')} {'DRY ' if DRY else ''}{m}"
    if VERBOSE:
        print(line)
    if not DRY:
        open(LOG, "a").write(line + "\n")


def sh(*a):
    try:
        return subprocess.run(a, capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=60).stdout.strip()
    except Exception:
        return ""


def rd(p):
    try:
        return open(p).read()
    except OSError:
        return ""


def num(p):
    try:
        return int(rd(p))
    except ValueError:
        return 0


def status(pid, key):
    for ln in rd(f"/proc/{pid}/status").splitlines():
        if ln.startswith(key + ":"):
            return int(ln.split()[1]) * 1024
    return 0


def procs(cgdir):
    out = []
    for pid in rd(f"{cgdir}/cgroup.procs").split():
        comm = rd(f"/proc/{pid}/comm").strip()
        if not comm:
            continue
        try:
            exe = os.readlink(f"/proc/{pid}/exe")
        except OSError:
            exe = ""
        out.append(dict(pid=int(pid), comm=comm, exe=exe, argv=rd(f"/proc/{pid}/cmdline").split("\0")[:-1],
                        rss=status(pid, "VmRSS"), hwm=status(pid, "VmHWM")))
    return out


def active_verilator_frontends(cgdir):
    """Read this scope's actual executables, not script names or an old cron phase sample."""
    names = {"verilator_bin", "verilator_bin_dbg"}
    return [p["pid"] for p in procs(cgdir)
            if os.path.basename(p["exe"].removesuffix(" (deleted)")) in names]


def frontend_waiting_on_build(cgdir, fpids):
    """True when every Verilator frontend pid in this scope has a build child (make / C++ compiler) in the scope:
    a --build verilator_bin whose AST phase is over and which only waits for the C++ compile"""
    if not fpids:
        return False
    parent, comm = {}, {}
    for pid in rd(f"{cgdir}/cgroup.procs").split():
        try:
            parent[int(pid)] = int(rd(f"/proc/{pid}/stat").rsplit(")", 1)[1].split()[1])
        except (IndexError, ValueError):
            continue
        comm[int(pid)] = rd(f"/proc/{pid}/comm").strip()
    waiting = set()
    for pid, c in comm.items():                      # walk each build process up to its frontend (sh -c make ...)
        if c not in BUILD:
            continue
        p, seen = parent.get(pid), 0
        while p in parent and seen < 64:
            if p in fpids:
                waiting.add(p)
            p, seen = parent[p], seen + 1
    return all(f in waiting for f in fpids)


def hist_rate(hist):
    """GB/s of RSS over the kept rss_hist window (>= 0), and the window span in s"""
    if len(hist) < 2 or hist[-1][0] <= hist[0][0]:
        return 0.0, 0.0
    span = hist[-1][0] - hist[0][0]
    return max(0.0, (hist[-1][1] - hist[0][1]) / GB / span), span


def is_sim(p):
    base = os.path.basename(p["exe"])
    return (base.startswith("Vtb_") or base.startswith("Vot_") or base == "vvp") and not p["exe"].startswith("/usr/lib")


_containers = None


def containers():
    global _containers
    if _containers is None:
        ids = sh("docker", "ps", "-q", "--no-trunc").split()
        try:
            _containers = json.loads(sh("docker", "inspect", *ids)) if ids else []
        except ValueError:
            _containers = []
    return _containers


def match_container(argv):
    hit = []
    for c in containers():
        cmd = (c["Config"].get("Entrypoint") or []) + (c["Config"].get("Cmd") or [])
        if not cmd or argv[-len(cmd):] != cmd or c["Config"].get("Image") not in argv:
            continue
        if any(b not in argv for b in (c["HostConfig"].get("Binds") or [])):
            continue
        hit.append(c)
    return hit[0] if len(hit) == 1 else None


def cdir(c):
    for p in (f"/sys/fs/cgroup/system.slice/docker-{c['Id']}.scope", f"/sys/fs/cgroup/docker/{c['Id']}"):
        if os.path.isdir(p):
            return p
    return None


def fresh_logs(c, since):
    out = []
    for b in c["HostConfig"].get("Binds") or []:
        root = b.split(":")[0]
        for pat in ("*.log", "*/*.log", "*/*/*.log", "logs/*/*/*/*.log"):
            for f in glob.glob(os.path.join(root, pat))[:400]:
                try:
                    if os.path.getmtime(f) >= since and os.path.getsize(f) < 2 << 30:
                        out.append(f)
                except OSError:
                    pass
    return sorted(set(out), key=os.path.getmtime, reverse=True)


def started(c):
    try:
        return calendar.timegm(time.strptime(c["State"]["StartedAt"][:19], "%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S"))
    except (KeyError, ValueError):
        return NOW


def route_proof(c):
    """a log written since the container started that shows detail routing has begun (GP and GRT are behind it)"""
    for f in fresh_logs(c, started(c)):
        if subprocess.run(["grep", "-q", "-m1", "-E", r"\[INFO DRT-0194\]|Start detail routing", f]).returncode == 0:
            return f
    return None


def in_gp_grt(c):
    """a log written in the last 15 min whose tail shows global placement / global routing activity"""
    for f in fresh_logs(c, NOW - 900)[:4]:
        tail = sh("tail", "-n", "200", f)
        if re.search(r"\[(INFO|WARNING) (GPL|GRT|RSZ|CTS|FLW)-|NesterovSolve|global_place|global_route|Running .*(place|grt)", tail):
            return f
    return None


GENERIC = {"run.sh", "run_case.sh", "stage.sh", "run.py", "go.sh", "job.sh", "main.sh", "run_all.sh"}


def classify(argv):
    """command class for the size table: script basename + first plain argument, numbers and hashes normalised"""
    a = list(argv)
    norm = lambda s: re.sub(r"[0-9a-f]{7,}|\d+", "#", s)
    if a and os.path.basename(a[0]) == "docker" and "run" in a[:3]:
        img = next((i for i, x in enumerate(a) if x.startswith("openroad/") or "orfs" in x), None)
        tail = [os.path.basename(x) for x in (a[img + 1:] if img is not None else a[-2:]) if not x.startswith("-")]
        script = next((x for x in reversed(tail) if "." in x), tail[-1] if tail else "?")
        work = next((x.split(":")[0] for x in a if x.endswith(":/work") or x.endswith(":/work:ro")), "")
        m = re.search(r"closure-loop/([A-Za-z0-9_]+?)[-_][^/]*/routes", work)
        return "docker:" + norm(script) + (":" + m.group(1) if m else "")
    while a:
        b = os.path.basename(a[0])
        if b in ("env", "nice", "stdbuf", "nohup") or "=" in a[0] and not a[0].startswith("/"):
            a = a[1:]
        elif b in ("time", "timeout"):
            a = a[1:]
            while a and (a[0].startswith("-") or a[0].startswith("MAXRSS") or re.fullmatch(r"%\w|\d+[smh]?", a[0])):
                a = a[1:]
        elif b in ("bash", "sh", "python3", "python"):
            a = a[1:]
            if a and a[0] == "-c":
                # v7 (ROOT 2026-10-16): the pass re-classifies from admit.log's space-joined command, so the -c script
                # arrives split into words; take ALL remaining words (a real argv has the script as one word, and its
                # positional parameters are rare), else every `bash -c 'echo ...; ... synth_master.sh'` was 'echo'
                a = " ".join(a[1:]).replace(";", " ").replace("&&", " ").split() if len(a) > 1 else []
                a = [x for x in a if x not in ("export",) and not x.startswith("PATH=")]
            while a and a[0].startswith("-"):
                a = a[1:]
        else:
            break
    k = next((i for i, x in enumerate(a[:160]) if re.search(r"\.(sh|py)$", x)), None)  # `cd X && VAR=1 bash run.sh ...`
    if k is not None:
        a = a[k:]
    if not a:
        return "?"
    cls = norm(os.path.basename(a[0]))
    if cls in GENERIC and os.path.basename(os.path.dirname(a[0].rstrip("/"))):
        # v7: run.sh / run_case.sh / stage.sh name a different job in every directory (one 421 GB run.sh made every
        # `bash case/run.sh` die case a 463 GB young charge): the parent directory is part of the class
        cls = norm(os.path.basename(os.path.dirname(a[0].rstrip("/")))) + "/" + cls
    for i, x in enumerate(a[1:6]):
        if x in ("--name", "--seq", "--shape") and i + 2 < len(a):
            return cls + ":" + norm(a[i + 2])
    plain = [x for x in a[1:3] if not x.startswith("-") and "/" not in x and not x.isdigit()]
    return cls + (":" + norm(plain[0]) if plain else "")


def launches():
    out = {}
    for ln in rd(f"{D}/admit.log").splitlines()[-4000:]:
        m = re.match(r"\S+ (oth-\S+) mem (\d+)G avail \d+G grow \d+G: (.*)", ln)
        if m:
            out[m.group(1)] = (int(m.group(2)), m.group(3))
    return out


def sizes():
    """local table merged with the fleet table (which contains this host's rows too: max, not sum)"""
    t = {}
    for p in (SIZES, FLEET):
        try:
            d = json.load(open(p))
        except (OSError, ValueError):
            continue
        for c, e in d.items():
            o = t.setdefault(c, dict(n=0, live=0, proved=0, peak_gb=0.0, req_gb=0))
            for k in o:
                o[k] = max(o[k], e.get(k, 0))
    for e in t.values():
        e["suggest_gb"] = math.ceil(max(e["peak_gb"] * 1.25, e["peak_gb"] + 4))
    return t


def admit_size(mem, cls, table=None):
    """(GB charged, why) when a request is over 2x the measured peak of its class, else None"""
    e = (sizes() if table is None else table).get(cls)
    if cls not in ("?", "cd") and (not e or e["n"] + e.get("proved", 0) < 1):
        for pre, gb in SEED.items():
            if cls.startswith(pre):
                fam, why = family_seed(cls, pre, table if table is not None else sizes())
                gb = max(gb, fam)
                if gb < mem:
                    return gb, f"family '{pre}*' seed {gb:g}G ({why}; class '{cls}' not measured yet)"
                return None
    if cls in ("?", "cd") or not e or e["n"] + e.get("proved", 0) < 1 or mem <= 2 * e["peak_gb"]:
        return None
    res = math.ceil(max(1.5 * e["peak_gb"], e["peak_gb"] + 8))
    if res >= mem:
        return None
    return res, f"class '{cls}' measured peak {e['peak_gb']}G, n={e['n']}+{e.get('proved', 0)} proved"


def family_seed(cls, pre, table):
    """v17.4 (coordinator 10-22 (c)): GB charged to an unmeasured class of a seeded family.  ep9 16:06-16:12: three
    192 GB qfd ref_gates were admitted at the 10 GB family seed while their openroad GRT reached 80-84 GB.  The seed is
    the 75th percentile of the measured peaks of its sibling classes (same first SEED_STEM_TOKENS '_' tokens, e.g.
    'ref_gate_qfd_c': p50 105 GB) when >= 2 are measured, else the one sibling, else the family's 90th percentile."""
    meas = lambda c, e: c.startswith(pre) and e["n"] + e.get("proved", 0) >= 1 and e["peak_gb"] > 0
    stem = "_".join(cls.split("_")[:int(conf("SEED_STEM_TOKENS"))])
    sib = sorted(e["peak_gb"] for c, e in table.items() if meas(c, e) and c != cls and c.startswith(stem + "_"))
    if sib:
        v = sib[min(len(sib) - 1, int(0.75 * len(sib)))]
        return math.ceil(v), f"siblings '{stem}_*' p75 {v}G of {len(sib)}"
    fam = sorted(e["peak_gb"] for c, e in table.items() if meas(c, e))
    if fam:
        v = fam[min(len(fam) - 1, int(0.9 * len(fam)))]
        return math.ceil(v), f"family p90 {v}G of {len(fam)}"
    return 0, "no family measurement"


GROW_SCRIPTS = re.compile(r"/(global_place|global_route|detail_route|detailed_route)\.tcl\b")


def growth_phase(procs_all):
    """v17.4 (coordinator 10-22 (b)): 'vl' while a Verilator frontend or its C++ compile runs, 'or' while an openroad
    GPL / GRT / DRT step runs, else '' (settled: no margin).  compiling = a cc1plus/cc1 is running."""
    comms = {p["comm"] for p in procs_all}
    if comms & {"verilator_bin", "verilator_bin_dbg", "cc1plus", "cc1"}:
        return "vl", bool(comms & {"cc1plus", "cc1"})
    if any(p["comm"] == "openroad" and GROW_SCRIPTS.search(" ".join(p["argv"])) for p in procs_all):
        return "or", False
    return "", False


def rebuild_sizes(st):
    t = {}
    rows = [ln.split("\t") for ln in rd(PEAKS).splitlines()]
    rows = [(r[2], float(r[4]), int(r[3]), "done") for r in rows if len(r) >= 5]
    rows += [(s["cls"], s["peak"], s["launch"], "live") for s in st.values() if s.get("cls") and s.get("age", 0) > 1800]
    rows += [(s["cls"], s["peak"], s["launch"], "proved") for s in st.values() if s.get("cls") and s.get("past_peak")]
    for cls, peak, req, kind in rows:
        peak = min(peak, req) if req > 0 else peak     # a unit cannot have held more than its MemoryMax (v6)
        e = t.setdefault(cls, dict(n=0, live=0, proved=0, peak_gb=0.0, req_gb=0))
        e["n" if kind == "done" else kind] += 1
        e["peak_gb"] = round(max(e["peak_gb"], peak), 1)
        e["req_gb"] = max(e["req_gb"], req)
    for e in t.values():
        e["suggest_gb"] = math.ceil(max(e["peak_gb"] * 1.25, e["peak_gb"] + 4))
    json.dump(t, open(SIZES + ".tmp", "w"), indent=0, sort_keys=True)
    os.replace(SIZES + ".tmp", SIZES)
    return t


def set_res(f, unit, old, new):
    """rewrite one reservation under the admission lock; only if it still says what we read"""
    with open(LOCK, "a") as lk:
        fcntl.flock(lk, fcntl.LOCK_EX)
        if rd(f).split() != [unit, str(old)]:
            return False
        tmp = f"{D}/.reconcile.{unit}.tmp"
        open(tmp, "w").write(f"{unit} {new}\n")
        os.replace(tmp, f)
    return True


def scope_cg(unit):
    cg = sh("systemctl", "--user", "show", f"{unit}.scope", "-p", "ControlGroup", "--value")
    return f"/sys/fs/cgroup{cg}" if cg and os.path.isdir(f"/sys/fs/cgroup{cg}") else None


def main():
    try:
        st = json.load(open(STATE))
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        st = {}
    if sh("systemctl", "--user", "is-system-running") == "":
        log("no user systemd bus: pass skipped")       # never wipe the state because the bus is unreachable
        return
    la = launches()
    table = sizes()
    freed, seen = 0, set()
    for f in sorted(glob.glob(f"{D}/res.*")):
        try:
            unit, m = rd(f).split()
            m = int(m)
        except ValueError:
            continue
        cg = scope_cg(unit)
        if not cg:
            continue
        seen.add(unit)
        launch, cmd = la.get(unit, (m, ""))
        s = st.setdefault(unit, dict(samples=[], first=NOW))
        s["launch"] = max(launch, m, s.get("launch", 0))
        s.setdefault("first", NOW)
        for x in s["samples"]:                          # samples written by v1 keyed a simulation as [[exe, 0], ...]
            if x[2] and isinstance(x[2][0], list):
                x[2] = sorted({os.path.basename(k[0]) for k in x[2]})
        ps = procs(cg)
        cs = [c for c in (match_container(p["argv"]) for p in ps if p["comm"] == "docker" and "run" in p["argv"][:3]) if c]
        ndock = sum(1 for p in ps if p["comm"] == "docker" and "run" in p["argv"][:3])
        cdirs = [d for d in map(cdir, cs) if d]
        cps = [p for d in cdirs for p in procs(d)]
        allp = ps + cps
        rss = sum(p["rss"] for p in allp)
        hwm = sum(p["hwm"] for p in allp)
        cuse = sum(num(d + "/memory.current") for d in cdirs)
        cgpeak = num(cg + "/memory.peak") + sum(num(d + "/memory.peak") for d in cdirs)
        if s.get("cls") in ("cd", "?"):
            s["cls"] = None
        s["cls"] = s.get("cls") or (classify(cmd.split() if cmd else ps[0]["argv"]) if (cmd or ps) else "?")
        # v6: the cgroup peak is the measurement; the sum of the live processes' VmHWM (peaks at different times, shared
        # pages counted per process) read 105 GB for builds whose cgroup never passed 57 GB and went into the class table
        s["peak"] = round(max(s.get("cgpeak", 0), cgpeak / GB), 2) if cgpeak else round(max(s.get("peak", 0), hwm / GB), 2)
        s["cgpeak"] = s["peak"] if cgpeak else s.get("cgpeak", 0)
        s["age"] = NOW - s.get("first", NOW)
        if not DRY:
            open(f"{D}/.use.{unit}.tmp", "w").write(f"{cuse // GB}\n")
            os.replace(f"{D}/.use.{unit}.tmp", f"{D}/use.{unit}")
        comms = sorted({p["comm"] for p in allp})
        # v17.4 (a): the current docker step's peak = the highest scope + container process RSS sampled while the
        # current set of containers runs (reset when it changes; a finished step's peak is not carried).  RSS, not the
        # containers' memory.peak: that counts their page cache (ep5 17:48: +418 GB of reclaimable cache).  (b) phase
        # A step is one set of containers in one growth phase: a Verilator build that finished compiling and now
        # simulates (phase 'vl' -> '') or an ORFS step that left GRT starts a new step; its peak is not carried.
        ph, s["compiling"] = growth_phase(allp)
        step = [sorted(cs), ph]
        if s.get("step") != step:
            s["step"], s["step_rss_gb"] = step, 0.0
        s["phase"] = ph
        s["step_rss_gb"] = round(max(float(s.get("step_rss_gb") or 0.0), rss / GB), 2)
        building = sorted({p["comm"] for p in allp if p["comm"] in BUILD})
        sims = [p for p in ps if is_sim(p)]
        others = [p for p in allp if not is_sim(p) and p["comm"] not in WRAPPERS]
        key = sorted({os.path.basename(p["exe"]) for p in sims}) if sims and not others else ["*"]
        s["samples"] = [x for x in s["samples"] if x[2] == key and NOW - x[0] <= 3 * FLAT_S] + [[NOW, rss, key]]
        span = NOW - s["samples"][0][0]
        vals = [x[1] for x in s["samples"]]
        flat = max(vals) - min(vals) <= max(0.05 * max(vals), GB // 2)
        # v13 GROWTH RATE (SCHED-TUNE 10-21): s["samples"] is wiped on every pass that sees a compiler / GRT / a new
        # process key, so it never held an RSS delta for a building job.  rss_hist keeps the last 3 cron samples of
        # scope + container RSS, never reset; rate_gbs = GB/s between the last two when RSS rose > max(5 %, 0.5 GiB).
        # v14: keep the whole 30-min window (the OLD SLOW rate); the v13 rate below still reads only the last two
        h = [x for x in s.get("rss_hist", []) if NOW - x[0] <= 3 * FLAT_S][-40:] + [[NOW, rss]]
        s["rss_hist"] = h
        (t0, r0), (t1, r1) = h[-2] if len(h) >= 2 else h[-1], h[-1]
        rose = len(h) >= 2 and t1 > t0 and r1 - r0 > max(0.05 * r0, GB // 2)
        s["rate_gbs"] = round((r1 - r0) / GB / (t1 - t0), 6) if rose else 0.0
        s["growing"] = rose
        kind, peak, why = None, max(hwm, max(vals)), f"procs {comms}"
        fast = bool(FAST.match(s["cls"] or ""))
        if fast:                                           # v4: gate families, lowered whatever runs inside
            peak = max(peak, cgpeak)
            if len(vals) >= 2 and span >= FAST_S and flat:
                kind, why = "fast", f"RSS flat {min(vals)/GB:.2f}..{max(vals)/GB:.2f} GiB over {span/60:.0f} min, procs {comms}"
            else:
                why = f"waiting for the 3-min flat window ({span/60:.0f} min, flat={flat}), procs {comms}"
        elif building:
            s["samples"], why = [], f"building ({building})"
        elif ndock != len(cs) or len(cdirs) != len(cs):
            why = f"docker job without a unique container ({len(cs)}/{ndock})"
        elif cs and "grt" in (cmd + " ".join(str(c["Config"].get("Cmd")) + str(c["HostConfig"].get("Binds")) for c in cs)).lower() \
                and not all(route_proof(c) for c in cs):
            s["samples"], why = [], "GRT job (never lowered before detail route)"
        elif cs and all(route_proof(c) for c in cs):
            kind, peak = "route", max(cgpeak, peak)
            why = f"{len(cs)} container(s) in detail route, cgroup memory.peak {cgpeak/GB:.2f} GiB"
        elif cs and any(any(p["comm"] in ("make", "yosys") for p in procs(cdir(c))) for c in cs):
            why = "flow container not yet in detail route"
        elif cs and (g := next((x for x in map(in_gp_grt, cs) if x), None)):
            s["samples"], why = [], f"container in placement/GRT ({g})"
        elif sims and not others and len(vals) >= 2 and span >= 240:
            kind, why = "sim", f"build finished, simulation {key} for {span/60:.0f} min, RSS {min(vals)/GB:.2f}..{max(vals)/GB:.2f} GiB"
        elif span >= FLAT_S and flat:
            kind, why = "flat", f"RSS flat {min(vals)/GB:.2f}..{max(vals)/GB:.2f} GiB over {span/60:.0f} min, procs {comms}"
        else:
            why = f"waiting for flat window ({span/60:.0f} min, flat={flat}), procs {comms}"
        if s.get("lowered") is None and m < s["launch"]:     # admitted on its class size by ot-heavy v4
            s["lowered"], s["by_class"] = m, True
        if s.get("lowered") is not None and m == s["lowered"] and \
                (rss > 0.8 * m * GB or (building and not s.get("by_class"))):
            # v5 (coordinator 2026-10-13 14:05): restoring the full launch value fought ot-heavy-trim (trim charges
            # observed use + margin, so RSS > 80 % of the charge at once, and every unit went back to its request:
            # 1,131 GB reserved against 787 GB available on EPYC1).  Raise in steps instead: to max(1.5 x RSS,
            # RSS + 8 GB), never above the launch value; the unit stays 'lowered' so the next pass can raise again.
            tgt = min(s["launch"], math.ceil(max(1.5 * rss, rss + 8 * GB) / GB))
            if tgt > m and not DRY and set_res(f, unit, m, tgt):
                log(f"RAISE {unit} {m} -> {tgt} GB (launch {s['launch']}): {why}, RSS {rss/GB:.2f} GiB")
                s["lowered"], s["samples"], s["by_class"] = tgt, [], True
            continue
        new = max(1, math.ceil(max(peak * 1.25, peak + 4 * GB) / GB))
        if (kind is None or new >= m) and s.get("lowered") is None and not s.get("no_class") and m == s["launch"]:
            a = admit_size(m, s["cls"], table)                # a full-size unit of an over-requested class
            if a and rss <= 0.8 * a[0] * GB:
                if DRY or set_res(f, unit, m, a[0]):
                    freed += m - a[0]
                    log(f"LOWER {unit} {m} -> {a[0]} GB (class) [{s['cls']}]: {a[1]}; RSS {rss/GB:.2f} GiB; {why}")
                    s["lowered"], s["by_class"] = a[0], True
                continue
        if kind is None or new >= m:
            if VERBOSE:
                print(f"  keep {unit} {m} GB [{s['cls']}] peak {s['peak']} GB: {why}" + (f" (needs {new})" if kind else ""))
            continue
        if DRY or set_res(f, unit, m, new):
            freed += m - new
            log(f"LOWER {unit} {m} -> {new} GB ({kind}) [{s['cls']}]: peak {peak/GB:.2f} GiB, RSS {rss/GB:.2f} GiB; {why}")
            s["lowered"], s["by_class"], s["past_peak"] = new, kind == "fast", kind != "fast"
    if DRY:
        return
    for u in [u for u in st if u not in seen]:
        s = st.pop(u)
        if s.get("cls") and s.get("age", 0) >= 240:       # finished: one row of history
            open(PEAKS, "a").write(f"{time.strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S')}\t{u}\t{s['cls']}\t{s['launch']}\t{s['peak']}\t{int(s['age'])}\n")
        try:
            os.unlink(f"{D}/use.{u}")
        except OSError:
            pass
    json.dump(st, open(STATE + ".tmp", "w"))
    os.replace(STATE + ".tmp", STATE)
    rebuild_sizes(st)
    if freed:
        log(f"pass freed {freed} GB of reservation on {os.uname().nodename}")


def meminfo():
    d = {}
    for ln in open("/proc/meminfo"):
        k, v = ln.split(":")
        if k in ("MemTotal", "MemAvailable"):
            d[k] = int(v.split()[0]) / 1048576
    return d["MemTotal"], d["MemAvailable"]


def scope_cgroup_snapshot(units):
    """One read-only systemd lookup, including scopes outside the usual app slice.

    Return None on unavailable/empty bus output so callers preserve the old
    per-unit fallback. A successful snapshot includes inactive scopes explicitly.
    """
    if not units:
        return {}
    try:
        result = subprocess.run(["systemctl", "--user", "show", "--property=Id", "--property=ControlGroup",
                                 *[f"{u}.scope" for u in units]],
                                capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=5)
        raw = result.stdout.strip()
    except (OSError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired):
        return None
    if not raw:
        return None
    out = {}
    for block in raw.split("\n\n"):
        fields = dict(ln.split("=", 1) for ln in block.splitlines() if "=" in ln)
        name = fields.get("Id", "")
        if not name.startswith("oth-") or not name.endswith(".scope"):
            continue
        if "ControlGroup" not in fields:
            continue
        cg = fields["ControlGroup"]
        if cg and not cg.startswith("/"):
            continue
        path = f"/sys/fs/cgroup{cg}" if cg.startswith("/") else None
        out[name[:-6]] = path if path and os.path.isdir(path) else None
    return out or None


def fast_cg(unit, snapshot=None, settled_inactive=False):
    """the scope's cgroup directory without asking systemd (a dozen file reads instead of one D-Bus call per unit)"""
    hit = glob.glob(f"/sys/fs/cgroup/user.slice/user-*.slice/user@*.service/*/{unit}.scope")
    if hit:
        return hit[0]
    if snapshot is not None and unit in snapshot:
        path = snapshot[unit]
        if path and os.path.isdir(path):
            return path
        # Do not reuse a negative snapshot for a live launcher or recent
        # reservation: nested-scope startup can race this locked read.
        if path is None and settled_inactive:
            return None
    return scope_cg(unit)


def read_units():
    """one row per reservation file: what the unit holds, what it peaked at, how old it is, what it may take"""
    try:
        st = json.load(open(STATE))
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        st = {}
    rows = []
    files = glob.glob(f"{D}/res.*")
    units = set()
    for f in files:
        fields = rd(f).split()
        if len(fields) == 2:
            units.add(fields[0])
    cg_snapshot = scope_cgroup_snapshot(sorted(units))
    for f in files:
        try:
            unit, m = rd(f).split()
            m = int(m)
            mt = os.path.getmtime(f)
        except (ValueError, OSError):
            continue
        meta = rd(f"{D}/meta.{unit}").split()          # written by ot-heavy v8: request GB, class
        s = st.get(unit, {})
        launcher = re.fullmatch(r"oth-.+-(\d+)-\d+", unit)
        settled_inactive = (NOW - mt > 120 and launcher is not None and
                            not os.path.exists(f"/proc/{launcher[1]}"))
        cg = fast_cg(unit, cg_snapshot, settled_inactive=settled_inactive)
        if not cg:                                     # not started yet, or finished
            rows.append(dict(unit=unit, res=m, active=False, file=f, file_age=NOW - mt, req=m, now=0.0, obs=0.0, age=0.0,
                             cls=meta[1] if len(meta) > 1 else s.get("cls"),
                             launcher_alive=launcher is not None and os.path.exists(f"/proc/{launcher[1]}")))
            continue
        cur = num(cg + "/memory.current") / GB + num(f"{D}/use.{unit}")
        mx = rd(cg + "/memory.max").strip()
        req = int(mx) / GB if mx.isdigit() else float(max(m, s.get("launch", 0), int(meta[0]) if meta[:1] and meta[0].isdigit() else 0))
        try:
            age = NOW - os.path.getmtime(cg)           # a scope's cgroup directory is created when it starts
        except OSError:
            age = 0.0
        rows.append(dict(unit=unit, res=m, active=True, file=f, req=req, now=cur, age=max(0.0, age),
                         # v17.4 (a): + the current docker step's container peak (the scope never holds the container)
                         obs=max(cur, float(s["step_rss_gb"]) if "step_rss_gb" in s else num(cg + "/memory.peak") / GB),
                         phase=s.get("phase") or "", compiling=bool(s.get("compiling")),
                         decl=float(int(meta[0]) if meta[:1] and meta[0].isdigit() else 0),
                         cls=s.get("cls") or (meta[1] if len(meta) > 1 else None),
                         sampled=bool(s.get("rss_hist") or s.get("samples") or s.get("first")),
                         rate=float(s.get("rate_gbs") or 0.0),
                         declared=max(req, int(meta[0]) if meta[:1] and meta[0].isdigit() else req),
                         frontend_pids=(fp := active_verilator_frontends(cg)),
                         frontend_waiting=frontend_waiting_on_build(cg, fp),
                         slow=hist_rate(s.get("rss_hist", []))[0], slow_span=hist_rate(s.get("rss_hist", []))[1]))
    return rows


